    "tpa_score_new": null,
    "tpa_score_new_en": null,
    "course_pol": null,
    "course_pol_en": "Expected classroom behavior\nStudents must arrive on time for class.\nCellphones, iPads, or computers are not permitted during class.\nAll students are expected to interact with respect in class and to behave reasonably, responsibly, and courteously at all times.\nStudents must listen attentively when classmates present or ask questions.\nWhen giving presentations, students must use an appropriate tone.",
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": "Diversity and Inclusion\nAll course activities will be conducted in an atmosphere of participation and interaction among students.\nStudents will respect and value each other's personal experiences and perspectives, considering different national and international school systems, diverse cultures, different learning levels, gender, etc.\nStudents will maintain high academic standards throughout the course and interact with other students with dignity and respect.\nOpportunities for exchange and constructive relationships will be fostered with and among students, with the aim of enhancing discussion and learning of the course content.",
    "ais_meno": null,
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>This is a BIBA course; students are expected to devote sufficient time to adequately prepare for class.</div>\n\n<div>Students are expected to participate in group discussions and complete assigned assignments.</div>\n\n<div>Copying texts without properly citing the source is not permitted.</div>\n\n<div>Plagiarism constitutes a serious breach of academic trust.</div>\n\n<div>For example, it is considered cheating to copy someone else&#39;s answers during an assessment or to turn in a paper or assignment that was written in whole or in part by someone else.</div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": "N"
  },
